        "ordinal": 0,
        "rIds": [
          "R1"
        ],
        "sourceRefs": [
          "spec",
          "rid-R1"
        ],
        "summary": "chart briefing is idempotent on a content fingerprint, but chart reopen changes nothing that fingerprint hashes - it only stales the briefing. Re-running briefing on the reopened chart therefore matched the old fingerprint and echoed the stale briefing back with noop: true, leaving a briefable chart with no capture-ready briefing and no path to one.",
        "taskIds": [],
        "title": "A reopened chart had no capture door"
      },
      {
        "files": [],
        "kind": "principle",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "rIds": [
          "R2"
        ],
        "sourceRefs": [
          "spec",
          "rid-R2"
        ],
        "summary": "A reopen is a new epoch, so a briefing emitted after one is a different briefing. Making the fingerprint say that routes post-reopen re-briefs through the ordinary emission path, which already mints the next B-ID, recomputes draft-vs-final, rewrites the convenience copies, and runs inside the existing WAL transaction under one lock. The epoch lives in _briefing_fingerprint and NOT in chart_decision_revision, which also supplies the tracker projection revision on every chart command.",
        "taskIds": [],
        "title": "Fix the identity function, not the return branch"
      },
